-- הסכם קיבוצי (17.9.2013) — "הסכם ספטמבר 2013": שעות פעילות גן, מחנכי
-- כיתה והקצאת שעות למורים בעלי תפקידים בחטיבות ביניים. For 27.8.2013 to
-- 30.6.2015, for the State's teaching employees in schools and the other
-- institutions of the reform: kindergarten activity hours, paid at 125% of
-- the hour value; the early end of kindergarten party days cancelled;
-- homeroom teachers using two individual hours for managing the class;
-- the grade coordinators' weeks of §§15(ה) and 17(ה) of the base agreement
-- replaced by role hours (§§15א and 17א); a choice between an hours grant
-- and tuition refunds for degree studies; negotiations on guidance roles
-- and on colleges; eight complexity levels for schools and new principals'
-- tables within a cost, the principals' pay frozen meanwhile; the next
-- wage negotiation; earlier agreements; exhaustion of claims, the end of
-- §155(א); and industrial peace.
--
-- It amends the base agreement of 25.12.2008 as the completion agreement
-- of 29.2.2012 amended it, so it imports what it changes and applies: the
-- base agreement's §§15, 17 (the weeks), 31 (the hour value, as §19 of the
-- completion agreement replaced its (ב)), 34 (study benefits), 66
-- (complexity levels) and 153 (earlier terms); the completion agreement
-- (coverage, kindergarten teachers' position base, §155(ב)'s populations);
-- the follow-up committee's decision of 12.3.2013, whose §3 §14(ו) here
-- continues; and the agreement of 22.7.2013, whose deferred allocation
-- §17(ד) meets.
--
-- The scan the corpus reads lacks page 5: §10(ב) breaks off in the middle
-- of the new §15א. The complete copy of the agreement the corpus also
-- publishes (`2013-09-17_ofek-hadash_september-2013-agreement_complete-cms-copy`)
-- prints the whole section and encodes it; here what is missing is a named
-- input.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `base-agreement-15`
IMPORT `base-agreement-17`
IMPORT `base-agreement-31`
IMPORT `base-agreement-34`
IMPORT `base-agreement-153`
IMPORT `2012-02-29_ofek-hadash_amendment_hascam-hashlama`
IMPORT `2013-03-12_ofek-hadash_vaadat-maakav_principal-pay-complexity`
IMPORT `2013-07-22_ofek-hadash_last-phase-deferral`

-- The day the agreement was signed.
`the signing of the September 2013 agreement` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 9 2013

DECLARE `September 2013 agreement action` IS ONE OF
    `prepare a work plan for the kindergarten activity hours`
    `approve the kindergarten activity work plan`
    `set how kindergarten activity hours are reported`
    `end the kindergarten's day early on a party day`
    `use up to two individual hours for managing the class`
    `allot role hours from the subject coordinators' pool`
    `continue negotiating the reform for teaching employees in guidance roles`
    `begin negotiating the reform for colleges and seminars`
    `hold discussions on the new principals' tables and the complexity levels`
    `begin negotiating the wage agreement toward 5776`
    `negotiate an additional economic demand for the 2013 agreement's term`
    `negotiate applying the cost of a Histadrut framework agreement`
    `strike or lock out over a matter the September 2013 agreement settles`

§ `הסכם ספטמבר 2013 — 17.9.2013`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The registration stamp under the Collective Agreements Law (6.1.2014, no. 244/2013); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 The date of signing, encoded above as `the signing of the September 2013 agreement`.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The first party, the State, and who represents it; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The first party's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p6 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 The second party, the teachers' union, and who represents it; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 The second party's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 A recital: the base agreement of 25.12.2008 and its short names ("ההסכם הכולל", "רפורמת אופק חדש", "הרפורמה"); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 A recital: the completion agreement of 29.2.2012 ("הסכם ההשלמה"); no rule.

-- A recital: the base agreement's agreed term runs to 1.9.2013 — the
-- day §4(ב) there sets (imported); this agreement's own term opens five
-- days before it ends (§4).
@ref akn:preamble/p12
`the base agreement's agreed term ends on, by the recital` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2013
#ASSERT `the base agreement's agreed term ends on, by the recital` EQUALS `the fixed term ends on`

-- akn:preamble/p13 A recital: the parties negotiated matters of employment under the reform and anchor what they agreed here; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

§§ `1 המבוא`

DECLARE `part of the September 2013 agreement` IS ONE OF
    `the September 2013 agreement's preamble`
    `the September 2013 agreement's body`

@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN p IS A `part of the September 2013 agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `binds as the September 2013 agreement` p IF
    TRUE

#ASSERT `binds as the September 2013 agreement` `the September 2013 agreement's preamble`

§§ `2 לשון`

-- "unless expressly stated otherwise": a word written in one form reads in
-- every other (the completion agreement's forms, imported).
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN `written in` IS A `grammatical form`, `read in` IS A `grammatical form`, `expressly limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a word of the September 2013 agreement reads in another form` `written in` `read in` `expressly limited` IF
    (NOT `expressly limited`) OR `written in` EQUALS `read in`

#ASSERT `a word of the September 2013 agreement reads in another form` `the feminine` `the masculine` FALSE

§§ `3 תחולה`

-- akn:art_3 The heading of §3.

-- Every employee on the teaching employees' scale in the civil service at a
-- school or institution: kindergartens, primary and junior high schools,
-- special-education schools and special-education classes in ordinary
-- ones, Matia centres, therapeutic centres, Pais clusters, Pisga centres,
-- agricultural farms, marine centres and kindergarten clusters — the list
-- the completion agreement's §3 names (its record, imported).
@ref akn:art_3/p1
GIVEN e IS AN `employee under the completion agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered by the September 2013 agreement` e IF
        e's `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`
    AND e's `in the civil service`
    AND NOT e's workplace EQUALS `another workplace`

#ASSERT `covered by the September 2013 agreement` (`employee under the completion agreement` WITH `ranked on the teaching employees' scale` IS TRUE, `in the civil service` IS TRUE, workplace IS `a marine centre`)
#ASSERT NOT `covered by the September 2013 agreement` (`employee under the completion agreement` WITH `ranked on the teaching employees' scale` IS TRUE, `in the civil service` IS TRUE, workplace IS `another workplace`)

§§ `4 תקופת ההסכם`

-- akn:art_4 The heading of §4.

@ref akn:art_4/p1
`the September 2013 agreement's period opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 27 8 2013
`the September 2013 agreement's period closes on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2015

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the September 2013 agreement's period` d IF
    d `is on or after` `the September 2013 agreement's period opens on` AND d `is on or before` `the September 2013 agreement's period closes on`

#ASSERT `in the September 2013 agreement's period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2015)
#ASSERT NOT `in the September 2013 agreement's period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2015)

§§ `5 הגדרות`

-- akn:art_5 The heading of §5.

-- The definitions of §7 of the base agreement, as §5 of the completion
-- agreement amended them, apply here, and so does any later change to
-- them: this agreement's words are read through those definitions
-- (imported), as they stand on the day a rule is applied.
@ref akn:art_5/p1
`the September 2013 agreement reads §7's definitions as they stand from time to time` MEANS TRUE

§§ `6 שעות פעילות גן`

-- akn:art_6 The heading of §6.

DECLARE `kindergarten activity under §6(ד)` IS ONE OF
    `staff meetings`
    `a one-on-one meeting with parents and the child`
    `an activity after kindergarten hours`

-- (ד): the kindergarten activities — staff meetings; individual meetings
-- with parents and children; an activity after kindergarten hours (a
-- theme party, an end-of-year party and the like). The list is closed but
-- for the third item's "וכדו'" (convention reading.closed-list). The
-- agreement of 19.10.2022 (§16.2) later adds a fourth.
@ref akn:art_6__para_d akn:art_6__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_6__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_6__para_d__subpara_3
`the kindergarten activities` MEANS
    LIST `staff meetings`, `a one-on-one meeting with parents and the child`, `an activity after kindergarten hours`

-- (א)–(ב): a kindergarten teacher on the reform's terms is paid for the
-- kindergarten activities 125% of the hour value computed by §31(א)(3) —
-- whose "school activities" read "kindergarten activity" and "teacher"
-- read "kindergarten teacher" — and §31(ב) as §19 of the completion
-- agreement replaced it: the combined salary and the pensionable role
-- allowances over her full position's weekly hours times 4.33 (imported).
-- Her full position's hours are her position base (30.4 in charge, 33.8
-- complementing; §133(ג) as replaced). No rounding is stated (convention
-- rounding.default). (ו): the same on her day off.
@ref akn:art_6__para_a akn:art_6__para_b akn:art_6__para_f
`the kindergarten activity rate` MEANS 125%

GIVEN p IS A `pay for the hour value`, c IS A `kindergarten teacher's charge`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the kindergarten activity hour value` p c IS
    `the hour value by the hours of a full position` (`the base of the hour value` `a school-activities hour` p) (`a kindergarten teacher's position base` c)

GIVEN p IS A `pay for the hour value`, c IS A `kindergarten teacher's charge`, hours IS A NUMBER, `on her day off` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pay for kindergarten activity hours` p c hours `on her day off` IS
    hours TIMES `the kindergarten activity rate` TIMES `the kindergarten activity hour value` p c

GIVEN post IS A `kindergarten post`, `on the reform's terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid for kindergarten activity hours` post `on the reform's terms` IF
    `a kindergarten teacher` post AND `on the reform's terms`

-- A teacher in charge on a placeholder combined salary of 7,600 with 0
-- role allowances: 7,600 over 30.4 × 4.33 = 57.74 an hour (to the agora,
-- for the check only); an hour of kindergarten activity is 125% of it,
-- on her day off as on any other.
`a kindergarten teacher's pay for the hour value` MEANS
    `pay for the hour value` WITH
        `combined salary`             IS 7600
        `special-education allowance` IS 0
        `pensionable role allowances` IS 0
        `a special-education teacher substituting in a special-education class` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the kindergarten activity hour value` `a kindergarten teacher's pay for the hour value` `the teacher in charge of the kindergarten`) EQUALS 57.74
#ASSERT (    `the pay for kindergarten activity hours` `a kindergarten teacher's pay for the hour value` `the teacher in charge of the kindergarten` 4 TRUE
         EQUALS `the pay for kindergarten activity hours` `a kindergarten teacher's pay for the hour value` `the teacher in charge of the kindergarten` 4 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `paid for kindergarten activity hours` `a paramedical kindergarten teacher` TRUE

-- (ג): the hours are allotted by the kindergarten's needs, never more than
-- 18 in a half of the school year; "לא יותר מ-18" holds 18.
@ref akn:art_6__para_c
`kindergarten activity hours in a half, at most` MEANS 18

GIVEN `hours the kindergarten's needs call for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the kindergarten activity hours allotted in a half` `hours the kindergarten's needs call for` IS
    min `hours the kindergarten's needs call for` `kindergarten activity hours in a half, at most`

#ASSERT `the kindergarten activity hours allotted in a half` 18 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `the kindergarten activity hours allotted in a half` 25 EQUALS 18

-- (ה): the hours are done by a work plan the kindergarten teacher prepares
-- at the start of each half of the school year and the kindergarten's
-- supervisor approves.
@ref akn:art_6__para_e
`the kindergarten activity work plan` MEANS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `prepare a work plan for the kindergarten activity hours`
    HENCE (PARTY `the supervisor`
           MAY   `approve the kindergarten activity work plan`)

-- (ח): how the hours are reported is set by the Ministry from time to time.
@ref akn:art_6__para_h
`setting the kindergarten activity report` MEANS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MAY   `set how kindergarten activity hours are reported`

DECLARE `when kindergarten activity hours are paid` IS ONE OF
    `with the next month's salary`
    `with a later salary`
    `not paid`

-- (ז): the payment is conditional on her report of the hours done and on
-- the supervisor's approval of the work plan. (ט): it is made with the
-- salary of the month after the hours, provided the report and the
-- supervisor's approval came in by the Ministry's deadline.
-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2013-a: (ט)'s proviso adds a deadline (ז) does
-- not set, and does not say whether one who misses it is not paid or paid
-- later. The reading adopted (convention reading.placement): the proviso
-- sits in the sentence that fixes the month, and decides the month — a
-- report and an approval that came in late are paid with a later salary.
@ref akn:art_6__para_g akn:art_6__para_i
GIVEN `reported the hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `the supervisor approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `in by the Ministry's deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `when kindergarten activity hours are paid`
DECIDE `when the kindergarten activity hours are paid` `reported the hours` `the supervisor approved` `in by the Ministry's deadline` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reported the hours` AND `the supervisor approved`) THEN `not paid`
        IF `in by the Ministry's deadline` THEN `with the next month's salary`
        OTHERWISE `with a later salary`

`the conditions §6(ז) names` MEANS LIST "דיווח", "אישור המפקחת"
`the conditions §6(ט) names` MEANS LIST "דיווח", "אישור המפקחת", "עד למועד שנקבע"
`§6(ט) adds a deadline §6(ז) does not set, and says no fate for a late report` MEANS
        elem "עד למועד שנקבע" `the conditions §6(ט) names`
    AND NOT elem "עד למועד שנקבע" `the conditions §6(ז) names`
#ASSERT `§6(ט) adds a deadline §6(ז) does not set, and says no fate for a late report`
#ASSERT `when the kindergarten activity hours are paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `with a later salary`
#ASSERT `when the kindergarten activity hours are paid` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not paid`

-- (י): on the payment, pension contributions to a provident fund for a
-- pension, 5% from the employer and 5% from her salary, on the principles
-- of the agreement of 17.12.98 (not in the corpus).
@ref akn:art_6__para_j
`the employer's pension contribution on kindergarten activity pay` MEANS 5%
`the employee's pension deduction from kindergarten activity pay` MEANS 5%

GIVEN pay IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pension contributions on kindergarten activity pay` pay IS
    pay TIMES (`the employer's pension contribution on kindergarten activity pay` PLUS `the employee's pension deduction from kindergarten activity pay`)

#ASSERT `the pension contributions on kindergarten activity pay` 1000 EQUALS 100

§§ `7 ערבי חגיגות עם הורים בגן הילדים`

-- akn:art_7 The heading of §7.

-- The option to end the kindergarten day at 11:00 on a day of a party with
-- the parents in the afternoon (Hanukkah, Purim, the end of the year), and
-- at 11:30 when Purim is celebrated in the morning, is cancelled: those
-- days end at the regular hour.
@ref akn:art_7/p1
`ending kindergarten party days at the regular hour` MEANS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `end the kindergarten's day early on a party day`

`a kindergarten party day may end at 11:00 or 11:30` MEANS FALSE

§§ `8 מחנכי כיתה`

-- akn:art_8 The heading of §8.

-- Notwithstanding §§15(ג) and 17(ג) of the base agreement, a homeroom
-- teacher may use up to two of the individual hours those subsections list
-- for managing the class, by the Ministry's guidelines from time to time.
@ref akn:art_8/p1
`individual hours a homeroom teacher may use for managing the class` MEANS 2

GIVEN w IS A `work week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the individual hours a homeroom teacher may give to managing the class` w IS
    min (w's `individual hours`) `individual hours a homeroom teacher may use for managing the class`

`managing the class in individual hours` MEANS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `use up to two individual hours for managing the class`

#ASSERT `the individual hours a homeroom teacher may give to managing the class` `a primary teacher's full week` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the individual hours a homeroom teacher may give to managing the class` `a junior-high teacher's full week` EQUALS 2

§§ `9 הקצאת שעות למורים בעלי תפקידים בחטיבות ביניים`

-- akn:art_9 The heading of §9.

-- (א): §17(ה) of the base agreement, the grade coordinator's week, is
-- struck out — from the agreement's period (§4) — and (ב) puts §17א in its
-- place.
@ref akn:art_9__para_a
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§17(ה) is in force on` d IF
    NOT d `is on or after` `the September 2013 agreement's period opens on`

#ASSERT `§17(ה) is in force on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 26 8 2013) AND NOT `§17(ה) is in force on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 27 8 2013)

DECLARE `coordinating role in grades 7 to 9` IS ONE OF
    `a grade coordinator in grades 7 to 9`
    `a social-education coordinator in grades 7 to 9`
    `a subject coordinator in grades 7 to 9`

@desc A teacher holding a role §17א (or §15א) gives role hours for, as far as the section asks.
DECLARE `role holder in grades 7 to 9` HAS
    `role in grades 7 to 9`                   IS A `coordinating role in grades 7 to 9`
    `classes in the grade he coordinates`     IS A NUMBER @desc for a grade coordinator: the classes of his grade, one of 7 to 9
    `classes the role hours are counted on`   IS A NUMBER @desc §17א: the classes of the junior high school; §15א: the classes of grades 7–9 in the school
    `hours the principal allots from the pool` IS A NUMBER @desc for a subject coordinator: what the principal allots him from the coordinators' pool
    `employed in a full position`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc FALSE for a part-time position or one with age hours
    `his week by the tables`                  IS A `work week` @desc his week by the work-week tables of §17 (or §15) for his position
    `frontal hours he teaches in the upper division` IS A NUMBER @desc §17א(ה): in an adjacent junior high, the frontal hours he does in the upper division; else 0

-- §17א opening: the week of §17 applies to them; their role hours, within
-- the school, are allotted by (א)–(ג).
-- (א): a grade coordinator of one of grades 7–9, the grade being of 4
-- classes or more ("4 כיתות ומעלה" holds 4), gets cumulatively (1) half an
-- hour for each class of the grade, at most 6, in place of frontal hours
-- (§17(ב)), and (2) half an hour for each class, at most the individual
-- hours in his position, in place of individual hours (§17(ג)).
@ref akn:art_9__para_b
`the classes a coordinated grade needs, at least` MEANS 4
`a grade coordinator's role hours in place of frontal hours, at most` MEANS 6

GIVEN r IS A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `his grade is large enough for role hours` r IF
    r's `classes in the grade he coordinates` AT LEAST `the classes a coordinated grade needs, at least`

-- (ב): a social-education coordinator, 0.4 hours for each class counted, in
-- place of frontal hours. (ג): a subject coordinator, what the principal
-- allots him from a pool for all the subject coordinators of half an hour
-- for each class counted, in place of frontal hours — at most one hour to
-- one coordinator. No rounding is stated (convention rounding.default).
GIVEN r IS A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role hours asked in place of frontal hours` r IS
    CONSIDER r's `role in grades 7 to 9`
    WHEN `a grade coordinator in grades 7 to 9` THEN
        IF `his grade is large enough for role hours` r
        THEN min (0.5 TIMES r's `classes in the grade he coordinates`) `a grade coordinator's role hours in place of frontal hours, at most`
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `a social-education coordinator in grades 7 to 9` THEN 0.4 TIMES r's `classes the role hours are counted on`
    WHEN `a subject coordinator in grades 7 to 9` THEN min (r's `hours the principal allots from the pool`) 1

GIVEN r IS A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role hours in place of individual hours` r IS
    IF r's `role in grades 7 to 9` EQUALS `a grade coordinator in grades 7 to 9` AND `his grade is large enough for role hours` r
    THEN min (0.5 TIMES r's `classes in the grade he coordinates`) (r's `his week by the tables`'s `individual hours`)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `classes the role hours are counted on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the subject coordinators' pool of role hours` `classes the role hours are counted on` IS
    0.5 TIMES `classes the role hours are counted on`

`allotting subject coordinators' role hours` MEANS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MAY   `allot role hours from the subject coordinators' pool`

-- (ד): (א)–(ג) are subject to the role holder's actual frontal hours not
-- falling below, in a full position, 12; in a part-time position or with
-- age hours, 50% of the frontal hours of the work-week tables and in any
-- case no fewer than 6 for a grade coordinator and 8 for a subject or
-- social-education coordinator. (ה): in an adjacent junior high (of a
-- six-year school), his frontal hours in the upper division count toward
-- the minimum.
@ref akn:art_9__para_b
GIVEN r IS A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the least frontal hours he must teach` r IS
    IF r's `employed in a full position`
    THEN 12
    ELSE max (50% TIMES r's `his week by the tables`'s `frontal hours`) (`the floor for a part-time role holder` (r's `role in grades 7 to 9`))
    WHERE
        GIVEN k IS A `coordinating role in grades 7 to 9`
        `the floor for a part-time role holder` k MEANS
            IF k EQUALS `a grade coordinator in grades 7 to 9` THEN 6 ELSE 8

GIVEN r IS A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the frontal hours counted toward the minimum, before the role hours` r IS
    r's `his week by the tables`'s `frontal hours` PLUS r's `frontal hours he teaches in the upper division`

-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2013-b: "בכפוף לכך" does not say whether role
-- hours that would take the frontal hours below the minimum are cut to fit
-- it or not given at all. The reading adopted (convention
-- reading.condition: a number set as a limit is no condition): they are
-- cut, to what leaves the minimum, and never below nothing.
GIVEN r IS A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role hours given in place of frontal hours` r IS
    min (`the role hours asked in place of frontal hours` r)
        (`not below zero` (`the frontal hours counted toward the minimum, before the role hours` r MINUS `the least frontal hours he must teach` r))

-- The role holder's week: the week of the tables, the role hours taking
-- the place of frontal and individual hours.
GIVEN r IS A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the role holder's week` r IS
    `a week of` (r's `his week by the tables`'s `frontal hours` MINUS `the role hours given in place of frontal hours` r)
                (r's `his week by the tables`'s `individual hours` MINUS `the role hours in place of individual hours` r)
                (r's `his week by the tables`'s `stay hours`)

-- (ה), its second sentence: the percentage role allowance is paid at the
-- rate for his employment in the junior high school.
`a role holder in an adjacent junior high is paid the junior high's allowance rate` MEANS TRUE

-- A role holder, for the examples: his role, his grade's classes, the
-- classes counted, the pool hours allotted, full time or not, his week by
-- the tables and his upper-division frontal hours.
GIVEN k IS A `coordinating role in grades 7 to 9`
      grade IS A NUMBER
      counted IS A NUMBER
      pool IS A NUMBER
      full IS A BOOLEAN
      w IS A `work week`
      upper IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
DECIDE `a role holder` k grade counted pool full w upper IS
    `role holder in grades 7 to 9` WITH
        `role in grades 7 to 9`                   IS k
        `classes in the grade he coordinates`     IS grade
        `classes the role hours are counted on`   IS counted
        `hours the principal allots from the pool` IS pool
        `employed in a full position`             IS full
        `his week by the tables`                  IS w
        `frontal hours he teaches in the upper division` IS upper

-- A full-time grade coordinator of a 9-class grade: 4.5 hours each in place
-- of frontal and of individual hours — but (2) stops at his 4 individual
-- hours.
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
DECIDE `a full-time junior-high grade coordinator of` classes IS
    `a role holder` `a grade coordinator in grades 7 to 9` classes 27 0 TRUE `a junior-high teacher's full week` 0

#ASSERT `the role holder's week` (`a full-time junior-high grade coordinator of` 9) EQUALS `a week of` 18.5 0 9
-- 14 classes: (1) stops at 6.
#ASSERT `the role holder's week` (`a full-time junior-high grade coordinator of` 14) EQUALS `a week of` 17 0 9
-- A grade of 3 classes: no role hours; of 4, two of each.
#ASSERT `the role holder's week` (`a full-time junior-high grade coordinator of` 3) EQUALS `a junior-high teacher's full week`
#ASSERT `the role holder's week` (`a full-time junior-high grade coordinator of` 4) EQUALS `a week of` 21 2 9
-- The week keeps its 36 hours less the hours given for the role.
#ASSERT `hours of the week` (`the role holder's week` (`a full-time junior-high grade coordinator of` 9)) EQUALS 36 MINUS 8.5
-- A subject coordinator gets at most an hour of the pool.
#ASSERT `the role hours given in place of frontal hours` (`a role holder` `a subject coordinator in grades 7 to 9` 0 27 2 TRUE `a junior-high teacher's full week` 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the subject coordinators' pool of role hours` 27 EQUALS 13.5

-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2013-b's evidence: a social-education
-- coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes, full time, is asked 12 role
-- hours by (ב); taken whole they leave him 11 frontal hours, below (ד)'s 12.
GIVEN upper IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `role holder in grades 7 to 9`
DECIDE `a social-education coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes, with upper-division hours` upper IS
    `a role holder` `a social-education coordinator in grades 7 to 9` 0 30 0 TRUE `a junior-high teacher's full week` upper

`a social-education coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes` MEANS
    `a social-education coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes, with upper-division hours` 0

`§17א(ב)'s hours would take a coordinator below §17א(ד)'s minimum` MEANS
    (`a junior-high teacher's full week`'s `frontal hours` MINUS `the role hours asked in place of frontal hours` `a social-education coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes`)
    LESS THAN `the least frontal hours he must teach` `a social-education coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes`
#ASSERT `§17א(ב)'s hours would take a coordinator below §17א(ד)'s minimum`
#ASSERT `the role hours given in place of frontal hours` `a social-education coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes` EQUALS 11
-- (ה): two upper-division frontal hours count, and he gets the 12.
#ASSERT `the role hours given in place of frontal hours` (`a social-education coordinator in a junior high of 30 classes, with upper-division hours` 2) EQUALS 12
-- A part-time grade coordinator whose tables give 10 frontal hours must
-- keep 6 (50% being 5).
#ASSERT `the least frontal hours he must teach` (`a role holder` `a grade coordinator in grades 7 to 9` 9 27 0 FALSE (`a week of` 10 2 4) 0) EQUALS 6

§§ `10 הקצאת שעות למורים בעלי תפקידים המלמדים בכיתות ז' עד ט' בבית ספר יסודי`

-- akn:art_10 The heading of §10.

-- (א): §15(ה) of the base agreement, the primary grade coordinator's week,
-- is struck out — from the agreement's period, as §17(ה) is.
@ref akn:art_10__para_a
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
